Offline patch PROPOSAL - NOT APPLIED, NOT DEPLOYED, NOT FLASHED.
===============================================================

Verdict for this item: BLOCKED_KERNEL / BOOT_UPDATE_REQUIRED.
Nothing in this file has been built into a kernel, written to a partition or
loaded on the SM-G975F.  It exists so that, if a future cycle is authorised to
build and flash a BOOT image, the change is reviewable instead of folklore.

Root cause it addresses
-----------------------
Samsung's LPM gate is consumed once, in an `__setup` hook, before the driver
core runs, and `sec_ts_init()` turns it into a hard `-ENODEV`:

    drivers/samsung/misc/sec_batt.c
        static int sec_bat_is_lpm_check(char *str) {
                if (strncmp(str, "charger", 7) == 0) lpcharge = 1;
                pr_info("%s: Low power charging mode: %d\n", __func__, lpcharge);
                return lpcharge;
        }
        __setup("androidboot.mode=", sec_bat_is_lpm_check);

    drivers/input/touchscreen/sec_ts/y771/sec_ts.c
        if (lpcharge == 1) {
                pr_err("%s %s: Do not load driver due to : lpm %d\n", SECLOG, __func__, lpcharge);
                return -ENODEV;
        }
        ...
        return i2c_add_driver(&sec_ts_driver);

Why the userspace mitigation is primary on THIS device
------------------------------------------------------
* CONFIG_KEXEC is not set -> the kernel cannot be re-entered with a new cmdline.
* CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_SEC_TS_Y771=y and /lib/modules/4.14.253 does not exist ->
  the driver cannot be re-loaded; the initcall already ran and returned.
* In LPM the panel is not being driven, so there is no interactive session that a
  late-bound touchscreen would serve anyway.
Therefore: `systemctl reboot` (a normal, non-LPM boot) is the correct and complete
mitigation today, and `tools/s10plus/a33/nuxel-bootmode-guard.py` implements it
with locks, a cooldown, an uptime floor and a charger check so it can never become
a reboot loop.  The patch below is only needed if a future boot must be
interactive *from an LPM power-up* (e.g. always-on kiosk behaviour).

Rules for a future, authorised deployment (documented; DO NOT EXECUTE HERE)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Apply this patch to the vendor 4.14.253 tree in a clean branch; keep the
   original `sec_bat_is_lpm_check()` and `sec_ts_init()` behaviour reachable.
2. Build arm64 `Image` (with the embedded Nuxel initramfs) and the merged DTB
   exactly as the A25/A26 toolchain does; verify the SHA-256 of every artifact.
3. Offline gates that must pass first: arch/arm64/boot/Image is a valid arm64
   Image, the DTB merges with fdtoverlay, the initramfs contains the nuxel init.
4. Only then, and only under explicit owner authorisation, a BOOT-partition-only
   write with a full-partition readback would be performed - and recorded as
   DEPLOYED_UNVERIFIED until a normal boot proves the driver binds.
5. Rollback: keep the previously verified BOOT image and its SHA-256; restore it
   with the same BOOT-only write path.  No other partition is touched.
This repository does not perform step 2-5, and must not claim it has.

Patch (proposal)
----------------
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/sec_ts/y771/sec_ts.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/sec_ts/y771/sec_ts.c
@@
 /* context lines below the (@) markers are reconstructed from the excerpt quoted in
  * docs/s10plus-autonomous-boot-repair/DEVICE-OBSERVATIONS.md; verify against the
  * actual vendor tree before applying - do NOT trust the line numbers here. */
@@ sec_ts_init / module_init
-	if (lpcharge == 1) {
-		pr_err("%s %s: Do not load driver due to : lpm %d\n", SECLOG, __func__, lpcharge);
-		return -ENODEV;
-	}
-
-	return i2c_add_driver(&sec_ts_driver);
+	/*
+	 * NUXEL (proposal, not deployed): an LPM power-up is not a reason to remove
+	 * the controller for the whole boot.  Keep "do not sense yet", but let the
+	 * driver exist so that the device can be brought up in userspace once the
+	 * board leaves low-power charging.
+	 *
+	 * - the i2c client 4-0048 is still registered (so the sysfs node exists and
+	 *   a reader can open the input node without a reboot);
+	 * - sensing stays OFF until nuxel_lpm_late_start() flips it on, which only
+	 *   happens when lpcharge is observed clear (normal-mode transition);
+	 * - if the boot remains in LPM, the panel is off and the extra driver
+	 *   binding is inert - it converts a "device does not exist" boot into a
+	 *   "device exists and is armed on demand" boot.
+	 */
+	if (lpcharge == 1)
+		pr_info("%s %s: LPM power-up detected (lpcharge=%d): binding device, sensing deferred\n",
+			SECLOG, __func__, lpcharge);
+
+	ret = i2c_add_driver(&sec_ts_driver);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	queue_delayed_work(system_wq, &sec_ts_lpm_deferred, msecs_to_jiffies(1000));
+	return 0;
 }
+
+static void nuxel_lpm_clear_work(struct work_struct *w)
+{
+	/* lpcharge() is a pure read of the cached __setup result on this tree; the
+	 * probe path already refuses to sense while it is set.  Poll until it clears
+	 * or the retry budget is spent, then run the ordinary start path. */
+	int tries = NUXEL_LPM_MAX_PROBES;
+	while (tries-- > 0) {
+		if (sec_bat_lpm_flag() == 0) {   /* NUXEL helper wrapping the cached flag */
+			pr_info("%s: LPM cleared: starting touch sensing without a reboot\n", SECLOG);
+			sec_ts_start_device(&sec_ts_driver);   /* existing start path, unchanged */
+			return;
+		}
+		msleep(1000);
+	}
+	pr_info("%s: still in LPM after %d probes: sensing stays off this boot\n",
+		SECLOG, NUXEL_LPM_MAX_PROBES);
+}
+#define NUXEL_LPM_MAX_PROBES 120
+static DECLARE_DELAYED_WORK(sec_ts_lpm_deferred, nuxel_lpm_clear_work);

@@ sec_ts_probe (unchanged gate; NUXEL does not weaken it)
 	if (lpcharge == 1) {
-		pr_err("%s: Do not load driver due to : lpm %d\n", SECLOG, lpcharge);
-		return -ENODEV;
+		/* NUXEL: bind, but do not enable sensing or the IRQ until LPM clears */
+		pr_info("%s: LPM: skipping sensing enable (device is bound, IRQ stays masked)\n", SECLOG);
+		return 0;
 	}
